{"format":1,"seq":566,"writes":[{"type":"entry","value":{"model":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'll tackle the pi-action guard PR first since it's smaller and in my own repo, then move to the pit PR. For the guard, I'm adding a running-env constant that marks when a pi-action is executing, and setting up the index to check that environment flag before running.\n\nIf the flag is already set, I should fail fast with a clear message about the nested run, implemented as a testable helper function. I'll also guard push.ts similarly for consistency even though the race there is less severe, since it's cheap to add.\n\nFor testing, I need to update the existing tool-env tests that use strict equality checks to account for the new variable, and verify the run tests still pass. I also want to document the new environment variable in the security docs where other toolEnv vars are listed, and branch off main with a name like fix/nested-run-guard since this is fixing a failure scenario rather than adding a feature.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Plan: the pi-action guard first, on its own branch from `main`, then the pit fix. I'll look at how the tool-env tests and docs describe the tools' variables."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_019xDMs87ypMJMbNxpyQud3A","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Switch to new branch from main and inspect tool-env tests/docs\"}\nasync ({ shell: { exec } }) => {\n  const r = await exec(`git switch -q main && git pull -q --ff-only && git switch -c fix/nested-run-guard && git log --oneline -1; grep -n \"GH_TOKEN\\\\|toolEnv\\\\|tool-env\" -r docs README.md src/*.ts | grep -v \"^src/tool-env\" | head -20; echo ----; sed -n 1,200p src/tool-env.test.ts`, { timeoutMs: 60000 });\n  return r.stdout + r.stderr;\n}"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"nvidia","model":"aws/anthropic/bedrock-claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":771,"cacheRead":113156,"cacheWrit